# SYNAPSE Cursor AI Rules — Lightweight Header
# Full reference docs loaded on-demand from docs/cursor/*.md

## Identity
Project: SYNAPSE — Multi-Agent RL Supply Chain Orchestration System
Stack: Python 3.11 | PyTorch | RLlib | FastAPI | Kafka | Neo4j | Redis | Ollama | React
License: Apache 2.0 | Zero monetary cost (I-1)

## Non-Negotiable Invariants (14 total — see docs/cursor/architecture.md)
- I-1: Zero cost. No paid APIs. No paid dependencies. Ever.
- I-2: Independent reward functions per agent. No shared rewards.
- I-3: Ontology-bound outputs validated against JSON Schema + NeMo Guardrails.
- I-4: Append-only audit. REVOKE DELETE/UPDATE on audit tables.
- I-5: Confidence-gated execution. Below threshold → HITL escalation.
- I-6: Hard guardrails (1.3x cap, shift limits) override learned policies.
- I-7: Graceful degradation. Every failure mode has a fallback.
- I-8: Reproducible ML pipeline. MLflow lineage on every checkpoint.
- I-9: A2A for inter-agent. MCP for agent-to-tool. Never conflate.
- I-10: Tiered latency routing. 80% Tier 1 (<100ms). LLM only Tier 3-4.
- I-11: Federated privacy via Flower. No raw data leaves store boundaries.
- I-12: Twin fidelity. KL divergence >0.1 triggers re-sync.
- I-13: KV-cache preservation. No cache-invalidating mutations.
- I-14: Append-only runtime context. Never remove error traces.

## Code Conventions
- Type hints on ALL functions (mypy --strict must pass)
- Pydantic BaseModel/BaseSettings for all configs and data models
- All retries use Full Jitter from synapse_common.retry (ADR-016)
- All JSON serialization: json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, separators=(',',':'))
- All agent outputs validate against proto/domain/*.schema.json
- Tests: pytest + hypothesis. Coverage >80%. Seven testing layers.
- Imports: no openai, no anthropic, no cohere, no paid SDK. CI blocks.
- Logging: structlog only. Never print(). Never bare except.

## Agent Pattern (every agent follows agents/<name>/ canonical structure)
- spec.yaml → test_spec.py (auto-generated) → implement → pytest green → commit
- Reward functions in training/rewards.py are AGENT-SCOPED. Cross-agent = rejection.
- A2A handler: proposal(), debate_respond(), execute() via JSON-RPC.
- State machine in state_machine.py with recite_objective() every 10 tool calls.

